{
  "comment": "Controlled zero-shot prompt bank for Tompkins Square Park. Tags are only recorded when a prompt clears its threshold; the CLAP embedding remains the primary representation, so a missing tag never means a moment is unsearchable. Prompts are phrased as CLAP was trained ('the sound of ...') and grouped so the softmax competes within a coherent set.",
